# New Feature Checklist

When adding a new feature to IndusJS Fleet, create files in this order:

## 1. Domain Layer (feature module)
- [ ] `domain/entity/{Feature}.kt` — clean data class, no annotations
- [ ] `domain/repository/{Feature}Repository.kt` — interface with Flow/Result returns
- [ ] `domain/usecase/{Feature}UseCases.kt` — one class per action, `@Inject`

## 2. Data Layer (feature module)
- [ ] `data/model/{Feature}Dto.kt` — `@Serializable`, `@SerialName` for all fields
- [ ] `data/model/Create{Feature}Request.kt` — request DTO if creating/updating
- [ ] `data/mapper/{Feature}Mapper.kt` — `@Inject`, mapToDomain/mapToRequest
- [ ] `data/datasource/{Feature}RemoteDataSource.kt` — interface + `@Inject` impl
- [ ] `data/repository/{Feature}RepositoryImpl.kt` — `@Inject`, Flow + Result pattern

## 3. Presentation Layer (feature module)
- [ ] `presentation/{Feature}Contract.kt` — State/Intent/Effect
- [ ] `presentation/{Feature}ViewModel.kt` — `@Inject`, MviViewModel
- [ ] `presentation/{Feature}Screen.kt` — Compose UI
- [ ] `presentation/{Feature}FeatureFacade.kt` — public entry point

## 4. Wiring (sharedUI)
- [ ] `FeatureRepositoryFactory` — add repository creation
- [ ] `DefaultViewModelProvider` — add use cases + VM factory
- [ ] `ViewModelProvider` interface — add VM factory signature
- [ ] `FleetRoute.kt` — add route(s)
- [ ] `FleetNavigation.kt` — add NavEntry with Facade call
